1
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa river,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:29,420
We were joking around.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,120
"Are you going again?" they laughed,
saying I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:45,940
Even if I leave some of my energy somewhere,
Katsushika is still here.

6
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:53,180
With a yawn, the unchanging
streets feel strangely gentle.

7
00:00:53,180 --> 00:01:01,180
From the pointed-hat clock tower,

8
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls into the great sky.

9
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end this way too, won't it.

10
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,140
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness is lost once again.

11
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:24,520
Because I'm a fool who
only just realized it.

12
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:31,420
Asakusa First Love Story

13
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:55,600
Ryo-chan. You're all dressed up for once.
What's going on?

14
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:58,040
Well, I just thought I'd
make a bit of an effort too...

15
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:01,260
Ryo-chan! What are you using?!

16
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:03,340
What's the big deal? Just a little bit.

17
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:06,000
But this is hair removal cream, you know.

18
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:06,720
Ugh, oh no!

19
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:08,680
Ouch.

20
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:12,720
Hey, this isn't hair mousse
or something like that, is it?

21
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:16,360
Honestly. You always go and use
other people's things without asking.

22
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:19,060
Senpai, I hear he's meeting his first love.

23
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,680
His first love? Ryo-chan?

24
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:26,080
Yeah, I've got a memory or
two of my first love too.

25
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:29,260
Come on, tell us, Ryo-chan.

26
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:33,640
What was your first love like, Ryo-chan?
Where did you meet her?

27
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:39,440
We met back when I was a kid, in Asakusa.

28
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:54,360
The Kaminarimon, burned in a fire
in the late Edo period, was rebuilt,

29
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:58,280
Sensō-ji's entertainment center, Shinsekai,

30
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,860
the twelve-story Ryounkaku tower,

31
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:04,080
and Hanayashiki,
all gathered together, made Asakusa

32
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:06,460
absolutely bursting with energy.

33
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,420
Back then,
even Hanayashiki had free admission,

34
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,980
so it was basically our backyard.

35
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:47,300
Coasters are still the
most thrilling and fun.

36
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:50,540
Hey, Kompe, didn't you wet yourself?

37
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:52,080
I did not!

38
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,660
Next, let's ride the Spitfire.

39
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:00,620
Hey, that girl's here again.

40
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:09,120
What's she doing at Dori?

41
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:10,420
Studying, maybe?

42
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:14,360
I heard she's an actress with
a troupe performing at Rock.

43
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,100
An actress?

44
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:17,580
Really? That's cool.

45
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:26,920
No, no, that's wrong.

46
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:28,200
Wrong.

47
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:31,980
How many times do I have to teach you?

48
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,980
Do you really think you're an actor?

49
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:37,340
Why can't you understand that you're
not supposed to do that impression?

50
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:40,480
It can't be helped.
We're changing Tate's blocking!

51
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:43,260
Cut Kotone's stage time!

52
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,760
Boss! Please, one more chance!

53
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:51,260
Dear, Kotone is working hard too, isn't she?

54
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:51,840
Out of the way!

55
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:54,600
Isn't she our daughter?

56
00:04:56,740 --> 00:05:00,440
An actor, no, on the stage,
there's no parent or child!

57
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:21,420
I don't know who you are,

58
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:23,600
but thank you for saving me back there.

59
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:27,140
At least, at least, may I ask your name?

60
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:29,320
It's Kankichi Ryotsu!

61
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:32,660
What are you guys?

62
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,140
Wow!

63
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:36,920
Hey, you two, look! It's a real script!

64
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,500
Sword fight, wandering bird, sword hand...

65
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:41,600
So the rumors were true.

66
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,780
You've been coming here a lot lately,

67
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:45,740
go away!

68
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:48,580
Go away!

69
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:50,480
Let's go, Kankichi.

70
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,721
Great actors like her

71
00:05:51,771 --> 00:05:54,640
apparently can't even talk to guys like us.

72
00:05:56,380 --> 00:06:00,180
But she's about our age and already an actress.
That's amazing!

73
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:03,620
I've never seen a stage script before!

74
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,700
Wait, did you talk to me
because I'm an actress?

75
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,440
We weren't making fun of you,

76
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:14,400
it's just that we've never
met a real actress before,

77
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:18,020
so we thought it'd be nice to talk, right!

78
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:18,520
Yeah!

79
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:22,800
But I'm not a real actress yet.

80
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:26,160
My acting's bad,
and I'm always getting scolded.

81
00:06:26,660 --> 00:06:30,560
We get scolded at school every day too,
you know.

82
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,340
Hey.

83
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,560
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu.

84
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:35,940
Kotone Tachibana.

85
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:38,520
Pity is lacking,

86
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:41,140
but sometimes it can be a cue, you know.

87
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:42,520
What's a "cue"?

88
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:44,480
Did you eat a pickled plum or something?

89
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:46,680
Write "kyuu" with the person radical,

90
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:47,920
and it's read "ada."

91
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:49,400
I see!

92
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,720
Hey, show me an example, will you?

93
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:52,600
Kotone-chan.

94
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:57,260
Miss, you mustn't.

95
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:58,860
A lack of compassion...

96
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:00,420
It can backfire, you know.

97
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:03,240
Well, leave this to me.

98
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:06,820
W-what, am I that bad?

99
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:09,860
Wow! So cool!

100
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,700
Kotone-chan, you look just like Ōkawa Hyōzō!

101
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:20,046
See, like this! Kotone-chan, someday you'll

102
00:07:20,096 --> 00:07:22,160
become a star like Hyōzō!

103
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:25,640
Ah

104
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:33,720
Prestigious and cool!

105
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,300
Admit defeat! Kankichi-nosuke!

106
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:45,900
Not yet, I won't!

107
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,200
Had enough, Kankichinosuke!

108
00:07:58,760 --> 00:07:59,480
Not yet!

109
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:03,520
Ahahaha!

110
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:06,220
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

111
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:07,640
Ahahaha!

112
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,140
Wait up!

113
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:10,780
Kankichi! Kotone-chan!

114
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,160
Where did those two go?

115
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:16,980
This way!

116
00:08:17,220 --> 00:08:17,380
Yeah.

117
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:22,140
Hehehehehehe

118
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:25,580
Hey, Kankichi!

119
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,540
Don't go stealing things!

120
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:28,600
Run!

121
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:32,220
Hey, there they are!

122
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:36,420
Yay!

123
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:40,880
We got one!

124
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:51,780
Wow, Kotone-chan!

125
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:13,979
My dream is to become
Japan's top stage star,

126
00:09:14,029 --> 00:09:16,100
and tour all of Japan with the troupe!

127
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,460
Kotone, you can definitely do it!

128
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:21,420
Kankichi's dream is

129
00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:26,260
to become a carpenter,
since he loves Osaka so much.

130
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:27,060
A carpenter.

131
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,220
Scratch that.

132
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:31,040
An airplane pilot.

133
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,760
Wow, an airplane pilot!

134
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:34,940
Scratch that too.

135
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:37,120
A movie director.

136
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:42,280
But I also want to become a manga artist,

137
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,240
I don't even know which one that is.

138
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:46,280
Sounds like Kankichi.

139
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:50,260
Speaking of which,
where are Chinkichi and Tonpei today?

140
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:56,060
Those two are stuck at school after class,
'cause they're idiots.

141
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:02,180
Damn it.

142
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:03,420
Once you've memorized them,

143
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:04,660
Kankichi.

144
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:06,160
Buffalo.

145
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:12,620
Kotone-chan's my type, so even being
alone with her makes me a little shy.

146
00:10:14,380 --> 00:10:15,980
I like you too, Kankichi-kun.

147
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:19,680
Saying you like me...

148
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:21,440
You got me... really.

149
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,080
Kankichi-kun, watch out!

150
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:33,720
Excuse me, samurai-sama,

151
00:10:34,460 --> 00:10:36,020
I don't know who you are, but

152
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,580
thank you for saving me from danger.

153
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,300
That Kotone,

154
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,020
she's let her shoulders relax,

155
00:10:42,020 --> 00:10:43,860
and she's started acting more naturally,
hasn't she?

156
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:46,400
It seems she's made some good friends too,

157
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:47,820
that's great to hear.

158
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:55,600
Kankichi-kun!

159
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:56,740
Kotone-chan!

160
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:58,700
Kotone-chan!

161
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:02,640
Dad says I can appear on
stage starting next week!

162
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:04,520
You did it, Kotone-chan!

163
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:09,480
I'll go watch from the very front.

164
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:11,700
Yeah, I'll do my best.

165
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:12,580
This one?

166
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:14,540
They say it's a new ride that's being built.

167
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:20,840
A 50-meter artificial satellite where you can see all of Tokyo?
How wonderful.

168
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:23,900
When it's finished,
let's ride it together first.

169
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:25,720
Promise?

170
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:26,340
Yeah.

171
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:29,920
Kankichi-kun.

172
00:11:30,620 --> 00:11:32,700
It's fine, come on, Kotone-chan.

173
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:35,080
The artificial satellite
is already finished.

174
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:40,140
Since she's a star,
let's reserve this gondola.

175
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:44,340
Let's quietly put a reserved sign on it.

176
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:46,760
On the gondola,

177
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,440
neatly and properly.

178
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:52,060
Nobody will notice here.

179
00:11:52,060 --> 00:11:53,300
Then lend me yours too.

180
00:11:58,640 --> 00:11:59,400
Uh...

181
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:00,980
We ended up sharing an umbrella.

182
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:02,680
W-well, w-well, w-well, never mind.

183
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:04,300
If anyone sees us, we're finished.

184
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:08,200
The storehouse is off-limits!

185
00:12:08,300 --> 00:12:08,720
Let's go!

186
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:17,340
Those two have gotten pretty
cozy without us noticing

187
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:17,780
Yeah.

188
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:26,640
She's late, isn't she, Kotone-chan?

189
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:29,700
Is today the last day?

190
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:33,660
But the performances were
supposed to run until next month!

191
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:38,680
Since Koyanagi-san has said it's over,
we have to go along with it.

192
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:43,060
If you're in this business too,
you know how things work.

193
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:44,320
No way.

194
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:48,180
We can't compete with
the Moji troupe, can we?

195
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:53,300
Suddenly putting on performances
just because the injury healed...

196
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:56,160
The whims of a popular
troupe are a real nuisance.

197
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:58,120
Above all, poor Miss Kotone.

198
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:02,100
She was so happy about getting
to perform on the Asakusa stage.

199
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:04,960
We have to leave here.

200
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:08,820
No way.

201
00:13:11,180 --> 00:13:11,600
No way.

202
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,540
Kankichi-kun.

203
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,080
Kotone-chan.

204
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:46,220
We finally became friends, and yet...

205
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:49,520
Thanks to Kankichi-kun,
I was going to get to perform on stage,

206
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:54,500
and I thought Kankichi-kun
would get to see my acting.

207
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:56,580
Always, always...

208
00:13:58,560 --> 00:13:59,280
Kotone-chan...

209
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:01,560
I'm sick of touring now.

210
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,340
I want to stay here forever.

211
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:04,840
I want to stay in Asakusa.

212
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,260
But then I can't become Japan's top star.

213
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:11,240
Kankichi-kun, are you okay with that?

214
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:12,900
Even if I'm the one who says it...

215
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:18,260
Otome-chan...

216
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:20,240
Me too...

217
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,940
I didn't want you saying it either, dammit!

218
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:31,940
Why did you have to go and say it?

219
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:34,400
We finally became friends, and yet...

220
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:47,260
Ugh...

221
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:49,240
K-Kotone-chan...

222
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:51,140
Ugh...

223
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,420
We have to ride it together, okay!

224
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:06,780
I'm looking forward to it!

225
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:21,220
Aaaaaah!

226
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:23,100
Aaaaaah!

227
00:15:23,100 --> 00:15:25,920
Aaaaaah!

228
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,440
Aaaaaah!

229
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:29,320
Aaaaaah!

230
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,480
Aaaaaah!

231
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:31,260
Aaaaaah!

232
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:31,820
Aaaaaah!

233
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:32,580
Aaaaaah!

234
00:15:38,580 --> 00:15:58,880
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no...

235
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:00,040
Kotone, we're leaving!

236
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:03,740
Kotone.

237
00:16:04,140 --> 00:16:05,460
How long are you going to keep sulking?

238
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:07,780
Fine, stay there and sulk
until you're satisfied.

239
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:08,980
Kotone-chan!

240
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:13,720
Kankichi-kun!

241
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:17,800
What happened, Kankichi-kun?
You're so dirty!

242
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:22,660
Mister, please.

243
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:25,100
Just give us some time.

244
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:28,500
We really have to show
Kotone-chan something!

245
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:30,020
Please!

246
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:35,340
Hey, Kankichi-kun,
what is it you want to show me?

247
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:36,420
It's almost ready.

248
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:03,360
I like Kankichi too.

249
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:22,780
We promised to ride it together first,
remember?

250
00:17:23,660 --> 00:17:24,580
Kankichi!

251
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:35,540
Hey, put me down.

252
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:36,720
You're such an idiot.

253
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:44,580
We borrowed this gondola properly, you know.

254
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:45,700
Don't worry about it.

255
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:47,440
Come on, get in.

256
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:54,000
Gondola, launch!

257
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:08,260
What you see straight
ahead is the Sumida River.

258
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:13,320
The big building you can see just before
Azuma Bridge is the Matsuya Department Store.

259
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:16,380
Beyond it, Asakusa Park stretches out.

260
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:21,740
Next to Sensō-ji, you can see the Ferris
wheel and flying boat ride at Hanayashiki.

261
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:25,640
The gondola will reach the top soon!

262
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:30,420
The sunrise...

263
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:37,080
Kankichi, you idiot,
putting on a brave front!

264
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:45,140
Kotone-chan...

265
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:48,640
I... I'll never forget this...

266
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:51,460
This Asakusa, and Kankichi-kun too.

267
00:18:52,160 --> 00:18:55,740
Kotone-chan,
this is as far as I can take you.

268
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:57,820
From here, you have to climb on your own.

269
00:18:58,360 --> 00:18:59,180
Kankichi-kun.

270
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:01,580
You've got to become Japan's star for sure!

271
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:06,200
Kotone-chan,
I'll always be cheering for you.

272
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:19,040
Goodbye

273
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:28,460
Good luck, Kotone-chan

274
00:19:28,460 --> 00:19:30,000
Goodbye

275
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:32,900
Goodbye

276
00:19:32,900 --> 00:19:34,460
Goodbye

277
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:35,340
Goodbye

278
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:38,680
Goodbye

279
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,420
Goodbye

280
00:19:48,280 --> 00:19:50,120
That satellite tower?

281
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:52,520
It changed into that "Beater" thing.

282
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,600
So you had a first love like that too,
Ryo-chan.

283
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:57,020
It's not like that.

284
00:19:57,020 --> 00:19:58,820
Don't be shy, don't be shy.

285
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:00,600
I'm not embarrassed at all.

286
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:06,120
So I had a normal boyhood like everyone else

287
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:07,380
Kankichi-kun

288
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,920
It's Kankichi-kun, isn't it?

289
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,100
Kotone-chan

290
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:16,600
So it really is Kotone-chan

291
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,500
It's been a while, Kankichi-kun.

292
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:24,300
I'm disappointed I've
turned into such an old lady.

293
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:25,820
You look lovely.

294
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:28,880
I'm amazed at how grown up you've become.

295
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:33,080
You haven't changed at all since back then.

296
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:36,980
Hehe, I hear Ichizawa is
super popular in Kansai

297
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:39,280
It's all thanks to you, Kankichi-kun.

298
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:41,359
About the play you sent us tickets for,

299
00:20:41,409 --> 00:20:44,020
Chinkichi and Tonpei couldn't
make it because of work,

300
00:20:44,020 --> 00:20:47,060
so I brought these junior
colleagues from work instead.

301
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:48,140
Hello.

302
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:53,373
Asakusa has changed quite a bit, hasn't it?

303
00:20:53,423 --> 00:20:54,360
Of course.

304
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:58,500
There aren't even any rickshaws anymore,
and nothing from those days...

305
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:00,340
Wait, there is one!

306
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:04,440
There is! That satellite from back then!

307
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:12,380
She's really gone

308
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:12,840
Yeah.

309
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:15,700
Alright, let's lower the gondola down!

310
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:17,920
Okay, let's go!

311
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:20,220
Be careful!

312
00:21:20,540 --> 00:21:24,120
Wait a second, Kankichi!
Shouldn't we put one more rope on it?

313
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:26,980
Alright, let's thread it through inside.

314
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:59,720
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

315
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:06,240
So that gondola from back then -

316
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:08,480
we never heard that it was ever pulled up,

317
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:12,540
so it should still be lying at
the bottom of the Sumida River.

318
00:22:13,620 --> 00:22:15,480
That's a very senpai-like ending, isn't it.

319
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:17,160
Really.

320
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:20,800
Thanks to you,
my nerves before the performance are gone.

321
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:24,040
Kankichi, you really are my savior.

322
00:22:25,220 --> 00:22:25,620
Thank you.

323
00:22:25,620 --> 00:22:25,920
Thanks.

324
00:22:28,140 --> 00:22:30,520
Heh, that's a piece of cake.

325
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:31,580
Kankichi-kun.

326
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:35,380
Well then,
I'll head back to the theater ahead of you.

327
00:22:35,820 --> 00:22:39,100
A dream nationwide tour!
Good luck, troupe leader.

328
00:22:39,100 --> 00:22:42,060
Yeah, more than any critic's opinion,

329
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:45,640
knowing Kankichi-kun is
watching makes me so nervous.

330
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:14,181
Samurai-sama,
though I don't know who you are,

331
00:23:14,231 --> 00:23:16,680
thank you so much for saving me from danger.

332
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:21,400
Well, who knows what would have happened.

333
00:23:22,380 --> 00:23:25,180
Acting in haste can sometimes backfire.

334
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:26,140
Excuse me.

335
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:29,400
Now, leave this to me. Go on, get going now.

336
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:31,760
Here we go!

337
00:23:34,780 --> 00:23:36,020
We've been waiting!

338
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:38,760
Hey, Kotone-chan, number one in Japan!

339
00:24:07,560 --> 00:24:09,740
Thank you for your hard work.

340
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:13,540
Hey, that's a problem, you know?
This guy really got fired up.

341
00:24:14,180 --> 00:24:21,660
Don't hide it, it's no good. Which girl is your favorite?
Next time, same deal, gamer, count me in on this.

342
00:24:30,620 --> 00:24:37,160
People rumor that I'm a
woman who can't fall in love,

343
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:42,020
but I have a mountain
of things I want to do.

344
00:24:42,020 --> 00:24:52,040
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

345
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:59,220
I want to be freer than a bird.

346
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:07,100
A lady's dreams that change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

347
00:25:07,100 --> 00:25:07,540
me

348
00:25:07,540 --> 00:25:09,860
me

349
00:25:11,100 --> 00:25:12,220
me

350
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:14,620
me

351
00:25:21,460 --> 00:25:22,860
me

352
00:25:24,340 --> 00:25:25,740
me

353
00:25:25,740 --> 00:25:26,960
me

354
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:27,660
me

355
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:28,400
me

356
00:25:35,220 --> 00:25:36,620
me

357
00:25:37,100 --> 00:25:41,100
Thank you for watching.

